<mujoco model="learn">
  <option gravity="0 0 -9.81"/>

  <asset>
    <texture name="grid" type="2d" builtin="checker"
             rgb1="0.9 0.95 1.0" rgb2="0.25 0.45 0.75"
             width="512" height="512"/>
    <material name="grid" texture="grid" texrepeat="12 12" reflectance="0.15"/>
  </asset>

  <worldbody>
    <geom name="floor" type="plane" size="2 2 0.1" material="grid"/>

    <light pos="0 0 3" dir="0 0 -1"/>

    <body name="falling_box" pos="0 0 3">
      <!-- if no freejoint, then it stays frozen where spawned--> 
      <freejoint/>
      <geom type="box" size="0.3 0.1 0.016" rgba="0.8 0.2 0.2 1" pos="0 0 0" mass="1"/>
      <geom type="box" size="0.05 0.05 0.010" rgba="0.1 0.5 0.4 1" pos="0 0 0.026" mass="0.1"/>
    </body>

    <body name="ball" pos="0 1 1">
      <freejoint/>
      <geom type="sphere" size="0.1" rgba="0.4 0.4 0.4 1" pos="0 0 0" mass="0.1"/>
    </body>

    <body name="pendulum" pos="0.5 0 1">
      <joint name="pivot" type="hinge" axis="1 0 0"/>
      <geom type="capsule" fromto="0 0 0  0 0.3 -0.1" size="0.03" rgba="0.2 0.4 0.8 1"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>

  <!-- TRY THESE, reload after each (this is how you learn the syntax).
       Press Backspace in the viewer to reset; Space to pause/play.

       BASICS
       1. change the red box mass="1" -> mass="50". Heavier = faster fall? (no — Galileo)
       2. change the box pos="0 0 1" -> pos="0 0 3". Higher drop, bigger bounce.
       3. change pendulum axis="0 1 0" -> axis="1 0 0". It swings on a different axis.
       4. delete the <freejoint/> line. The box now hangs frozen in mid-air
          (no joint = welded to the world). This is the #1 beginner surprise.
       5. add a second <geom> inside falling_box. One body, two shapes.

       MAKE THINGS MOVE
       6. make the pendulum actually swing: change its fromto to
          "0 0 0  0.3 0 -0.3" so it STARTS off-vertical, then watch gravity swing it.
       7. change <option gravity="0 0 -9.81"/> to "0 0 -1.62" (moon). Slow-mo fall.
          Then try "0 0 0" — the box floats, the pendulum never moves.

       SHAPES & LOOKS
       8. change the box geom type="box" to type="sphere" and delete two of the three
          size numbers (sphere needs only one). Now it lands and rolls.
       9. change the capsule size="0.03" -> size="0.08". A fat rod instead of a thin one.
      10. change the box rgba="0.8 0.2 0.2 1" -> "0.8 0.2 0.2 0.3". The 4th number is
          alpha — now it's see-through.

       THE FLOOR (asset practice)
      11. change texrepeat="12 12" -> "40 40". Many more, smaller squares.
      12. change rgb1/rgb2 to "1 1 1" and "0.6 0.6 0.6" for a grey/white Isaac-Gym floor.
      13. rename <material name="grid"> to name="floortex" but DON'T update the geom's
          material="grid". See the "material not found" error — names must match exactly.

       BUILD SOMETHING
      14. copy the whole pendulum <body> block, paste it, and change name + pos="1.5 0 1".
          Two pendulums. (This is how you'll add your 2nd wheel later.) -->
</mujoco>
